A word from [santiagosayshey](https://github.com/santiagosayshey), Profilarr's maintainer:

> I started Profilarr to scratch my own itch, and I keep building it because I enjoy it. Money doesn't really matter to me, and I'd much rather you put yours somewhere it matters more. The best way to support the project is to come hang out with us on [Discord](https://discord.gg/2A89tXZMgA), or to come help build Profilarr with us. See [Contributing](/docs/contributing) for where to start.

Every feature in Profilarr is free for everyone, and development will continue with or without donations. If you'd like to show support, you can, but it's in no way necessary.

